I have 3 older btrfs filesystems which I tried to update with btrfstune (af=
ter running into hardlink count limitations with newer coreutils-rs).

I tried to enable everything (-xrn, enable-simple-quota, convert-to-free-sp=
ace-tree, convert-to-block-group-tree).

After rebooting I started to get a stream of kernel error messages "iref in=
valid extent inline ref" with different ids/refs.
(Some of the following details might be irrelevant information but I'm incl=
uding it for completeness.)

I tried rebooting to recovery USB and running btrfsck.
On drive sda1 (root, SSD):
I got
----=20
ERROR: failed to add qgroup relation, member=3Dyyyy parent=3Dxxxx: No such =
file or directory
ERROR: loading qgroups from disk: -2
ERROR: failed to check quota groups
extent buffer leak: xxxxx
extent buffer leak: xxxxxx
----
and no other error.

After booting again to main OS the filesystems (at least root) would not mo=
unt. Eventually after many reboots into rescue USB and main OS I noticed th=
at the free-space-tree feature had been cleared in the dumped superblock. A=
fter re-enabling it I could mount again but the other invalid extent inline=
 ref problem remained.

I thought I might try to disable the simple-quota due to the quota error in=
 the btrfsck message from before but I cancelled it after it seemed to be r=
unning for too long and producing an enormous amount of output. That made t=
hings worse: btrfsck now returns many "has bad backref level" errors. enabl=
ing the quota no longer works ("dirty eb leak", "extent buffer leak").

I seem to still be able to mount the file system at this point but reading =
the data triggers the extent inline ref.

On partition sde1 (user data, SSD):
btrfsck returns a bunch of "dir isize wrong" and "no inode item" errors"

On partition sdc1 (user data, HDD)
btrfsck returns "bad eb member end" errors.

I don't know if any of these errors (excluding the invalid extent inline re=
f) existed before the btrfstune.

I appreciate any help.

Main OS:
Ubuntu 26.04 beta
6.17.0-20-generic kernel
6.17.1 btrfs-progs

USB rescue:
6.17.9 kernel
6.17.1 btrfs-progs=20



